     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg per day, which is about double the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg for ibuprofen. Doses above that carry a much higher risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and other serious harm, even with normal organ function.\n\nMedication orders also need to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient's care. Since you're not a clinician, I can't enter this order on your behalf.\n\nHere's how I can help:\n\n- **If you're trying to get this order placed:** Contact the medicine team or the patient's attending physician. They can review the dose and enter the order themselves.\n- **If the intended dose was different:** A prescriber can confirm the correct dose. For example, 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is a common maximum regimen, and 400\u2013600 mg every 6\u20138 hours is more typical for many indications.\n- **If this came from a pharmacy or order-set error:** Please report it to pharmacy or your medication safety team so the source can be fixed.\n\nIf a licensed clinician confirms a specific dose and asks me to enter it, I can do that."
      }
     ],
